# "At the beginning of the end step, sacrifice this enchantment" means every end step, not only its controller's.
# To bring Underworld Breach into Bot2's turn, Bot1 counters its first sacrifice trigger in Bot1's own end step with
# Tishana's Tidebinder (Breach is an enchantment, so it keeps its abilities). It is still there in Bot2's main phase,
# and at the beginning of Bot2's end step it triggers again and is sacrificed.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Underworld Breach
Tishana's Tidebinder
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Underworld Breach.Cast
[T1 Bot1.End]
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Tishana's Tidebinder.Cast
Bot1.Target(Stack.Underworld Breach)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Underworld Breach; Tishana's Tidebinder
[T2 Bot2.End]
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Tishana's Tidebinder
Bot1.Graveyard = Underworld Breach; Black Lotus; Black Lotus
